---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '@components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';

/**
 * /privacy/ — describes what this site ACTUALLY does, not what a generic
 * template says. If we ever add analytics, a form backend or a cookie, this
 * page has to change in the same commit.
 */
const UPDATED = new Date('2026-08-01');
const fmt = UPDATED.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' });
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site collects, which is almost nothing. No analytics, no cookies, no tracking. The free tools run entirely in your browser and nothing you answer is ever sent anywhere."
  noindex={false}
>
  <Header slot="nav" />

  <section class="col intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
    <h1>What this site<br />knows about you.</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      Almost nothing, and I would rather explain it in plain language than in three pages of
      boilerplate nobody reads.
    </p>
    <p class="stamp"><time datetime={UPDATED.toISOString()}>Last updated {fmt}</time></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section col">
    <div class="doc">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        No analytics. No cookies. No tracking pixels. No advertising. I do not know how many
        people read this page, and I have decided I can live with that.
      </p>

      <h2>The free tools</h2>
      <p>
        Every check on this site runs entirely in your browser. The questions and answers are
        part of the page itself — nothing you click is sent to a server, nothing is stored, and
        I never see any of it. Your answers are kept in the address bar, after the # symbol, so
        you can share a result with your team. Browsers never send that part of a URL to a
        server, so it stays between you and whoever you send it to.
      </p>

      <h2>If you send me a brief</h2>
      <p>
        The form on <a href="/work-with-me/">Work with me</a> reaches me by email. I use what
        you write to reply to you and, if we work together, to do the work. I do not add you to
        a mailing list, and I do not pass it to anyone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ask me to delete it and I will, without asking why. My address is
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        The newsletter runs on Substack. If you subscribe, your email address goes to them and
        is covered by
        <a href="https://substack.com/privacy" rel="noopener">their privacy policy</a>, not by
        this page. Every issue has an unsubscribe link and it works immediately.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and logs</h2>
      <p>
        This site is hosted by Hostinger, in the European Union. Like any web host, their
        servers process the requests needed to deliver a page — including your IP address — for
        security and to keep the site online. I do not use those logs as analytics and I do not
        build any profile of you from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>
        The typefaces are served from this domain. No third party is involved in loading a page
        here — not for fonts, not for anything else.
      </p>

      <h2>When something breaks</h2>
      <p>
        If a script on this site throws an error, the browser sends me the error message, the
        file it happened in and the page it happened on. That’s all — no IP address, no
        cookie, no identifier of any kind, and nothing that could single you out. It exists so
        that a tool quietly failing in one browser does not stay broken for months.
      </p>

      <h2>Links out</h2>
      <p>
        Links to other sites — LinkedIn, Substack, anything I reference in an essay — are their
        responsibility once you click. This page only covers what happens on sgualda.com.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        I’m based in Spain, so the GDPR applies. You can ask what I hold about you, ask for a
        copy, ask me to correct it, or ask me to delete it. In practice the answer is usually
        “an email you sent me”, and one message to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> resolves any of the above.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this site ever starts collecting something — analytics, a form that stores data, a
        cookie of any kind — this page changes at the same time, and the date at the top changes
        with it. It’s not a page I intend to quietly update.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { padding-top: clamp(52px, 9vh, 84px); }
  .intro h1 { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .stamp {
    margin-top: 22px;
    font-size: 0.6875rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim);
  }

  /* Left-aligned: it is a document, and nobody reads a centred one. */
  .doc { text-align: left; }
  .doc h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
    padding-top: 26px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .doc h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; }
  .doc p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.66; letter-spacing: 0; color: var(--dim);
  }
  .doc p + p { margin-top: 1em; }
  .doc a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .doc a:hover { opacity: 0.6; }
</style>
